  "important_behavior": [
    "Whole denominator intervals must exclude zero. Held zero factors and zeroth powers do not erase source-domain obligations.",
    "Native coth evaluates via 1/tanh(x); sech and large-argument csch use exp(-abs(x)) formulas; tiny csch uses 1/sinh(x). All emitted operation results must be finite before memoization/publication.",
    "Private numerical coth differentiation uses -csch(x)^2 to retain representable nonzero derivative tails that 1-coth(x)^2 rounds to zero. The independent reference verifier implements its own stable rule, including omitted sparse-zero admission. Ordinary symbolic diff and ordinary derivative receipts are unchanged.",
    "Both derivative stages, source identity, ordered typed variables, bytecode provenance, cumulative budgets, cancellation and atomic publication remain enforced.",
    "The ordinary math backend follows pinned SymPy 1.14 formulas and exception behavior, including large-argument OverflowError; explicit native evaluation has the stable formulas.",
    "Existing concurrent numerical-consumer commits were retained; no PR, forced ref update, broad profile closure or bead status/priority/dependency promotion."
  ],
